217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 168 0 R
/T (City traffic is growing every year, but there is still no complete, end to end system that manages it intelligently. What cities need is a system that handles rising traffic before it becomes a problem, not after. This matters because congestion is very hard to undo once it forms. By the time a jam has built up, almost nothing can clear it quickly. So, the real goal should be to prevent congestion from forming in the first place, rather than trying to dissolve it after the damage is done.)
/E (City traffic is growing every year, but there is still no complete, end to end system that manages it intelligently. What cities need is a system that handles rising traffic before it becomes a problem, not after. This matters because congestion is very hard to undo once it forms. By the time a jam has built up, almost nothing can clear it quickly. So, the real goal should be to prevent congestion from forming in the first place, rather than trying to dissolve it after the damage is done.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 168 0 R
/T (The trouble usually starts with a small bottleneck. Traffic keeps arriving and piling up at that point, and vehicles accumulate even on stretches where the flow should have been easing off. It behaves like water in a partly blocked drain. As long as more keeps coming in, it eventually overflows, and a jam appears even in places where one should never have formed.)
/E (The trouble usually starts with a small bottleneck. Traffic keeps arriving and piling up at that point, and vehicles accumulate even on stretches where the flow should have been easing off. It behaves like water in a partly blocked drain. As long as more keeps coming in, it eventually overflows, and a jam appears even in places where one should never have formed.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
