/T (Traffic congestion is not a niche infrastructure issue. It is a daily problem faced by each one of us. We sit in it, our families sit in it, and emergency vehicles get stuck in it. Indian cities lose an estimated $22 billion every year to congestion through wasted fuel, lost working hours and avoidable pollution. The number of vehicles on the road grows every year but the roads do not, and without a smarter way to manage flow, the problem only gets worse.)
/E (Traffic congestion is not a niche infrastructure issue. It is a daily problem faced by each one of us. We sit in it, our families sit in it, and emergency vehicles get stuck in it. Indian cities lose an estimated $22 billion every year to congestion through wasted fuel, lost working hours and avoidable pollution. The number of vehicles on the road grows every year but the roads do not, and without a smarter way to manage flow, the problem only gets worse.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 169 0 R
/T (Despite all the technology available today, there is still no complete, end to end system that manages city traffic intelligently. What exists is patchy, short sighted and reactive. Systems try to clear jams after they have formed, which is nearly impossible to do well. The real opportunity, and the reason we took up this problem, is to build a framework that prevents congestion from forming in the first place rather than struggling to dissolve it after the damage is done.)
/E (Despite all the technology available today, there is still no complete, end to end system that manages city traffic intelligently. What exists is patchy, short sighted and reactive. Systems try to clear jams after they have formed, which is nearly impossible to do well. The real opportunity, and the reason we took up this problem, is to build a framework that prevents congestion from forming in the first place rather than struggling to dissolve it after the damage is done.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
