/T (Today's traffic systems are patchy and short sighted. Most rely on cameras that can only see what is right in front of the junction. They react to congestion after it has already arrived instead of seeing it build up from a distance. Cities need a longer range view of traffic so the system can prepare in advance, not respond at the last moment.)
/E (Today's traffic systems are patchy and short sighted. Most rely on cameras that can only see what is right in front of the junction. They react to congestion after it has already arrived instead of seeing it build up from a distance. Cities need a longer range view of traffic so the system can prepare in advance, not respond at the last moment.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
