294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 175 0 R
/T (PRAVAH runs on a live digital twin of the road network, a continuously updated virtual replica of the real city, built in SUMO and kept in sync with the street through GNSS density and speed on one side and camera queue and vehicle-class data on the other. The twin is not a static map. It mirrors what the network is actually doing, second by second.)
/E (PRAVAH runs on a live digital twin of the road network, a continuously updated virtual replica of the real city, built in SUMO and kept in sync with the street through GNSS density and speed on one side and camera queue and vehicle-class data on the other. The twin is not a static map. It mirrors what the network is actually doing, second by second.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 845 0 R
/T (A mirror of the real road, not a model of an ideal one. OpenStreetMap gives the twin its geometry, and the fused GNSS and camera feeds keep every segment's density, speed and queue state matched to reality. The twin always reflects the network as it is, not as it was designed to be.)
/E (A mirror of the real road, not a model of an ideal one. OpenStreetMap gives the twin its geometry, and the fused GNSS and camera feeds keep every segment's density, speed and queue state matched to reality. The twin always reflects the network as it is, not as it was designed to be.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 846 0 R
/T (A place to understand before acting. The Digital Twin gives PRAVAH the network-wide insights and foresight needed to make better control decisions. It lets the system see how a decision at one junction will affect traffic across the network before that decision reaches the street.)
/E (A place to understand before acting. The Digital Twin gives PRAVAH the network-wide insights and foresight needed to make better control decisions. It lets the system see how a decision at one junction will affect traffic across the network before that decision reaches the street.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 847 0 R
/T (The environment where our light-placement model learns. The twin is also what makes mid-road traffic light placement possible. Our reinforcement learning model treats the twin as its training environment, trying out control points at different positions along the road and watching how each one affects flow. This is how PRAVAH works out where a new light would actually help, before a single one is installed in the real world.)
/E (The environment where our light-placement model learns. The twin is also what makes mid-road traffic light placement possible. Our reinforcement learning model treats the twin as its training environment, trying out control points at different positions along the road and watching how each one affects flow. This is how PRAVAH works out where a new light would actually help, before a single one is installed in the real world.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 848 0 R
/T (Foresight, not just observation. Because the twin runs faster than real time, PRAVAH can look a few minutes ahead, see a bottleneck forming before it exists on the road, and act early. This is the core shift from reacting to congestion to preventing it.)
